# The integration-layer CLI plugin (@commercetools-internal/cli-topic-integration-layer)
# is published to commercetools' internal GCP Artifact Registry. Map the scope so both
# `pnpm install` and `commercetools plugins install` resolve it.
#
# No token is committed here. In CI, Serenity provisions the GCP credentials and a
# short-lived _authToken is appended by `google-artifactregistry-auth`; locally,
# authenticate your own npm config the same way.
# See https://sd.commercetools.com/getting-started/continuous-integration/working-with-artifacts/
@commercetools-internal:registry=https://europe-npm.pkg.dev/commercetools-platform/internal-npm/
//europe-npm.pkg.dev/commercetools-platform/internal-npm/:always-auth=true
